            <ArticleTitle>Phenolic acid derivatives with neuroprotective effect from the aqueous extract of Clerodendranthus spicatus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>974-980</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/10286020.2016.1277707</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two new phenolic acid helisterculins C (1) and D (2) were isolated from the whole plant of Clerodendranthus spicatus. Their structures were elucidated on the basis of 1D and 2D NMR, MS, and CD analysis. Compound 1 possesses an unusual bicyclol [2. 2. 2] octane moiety which is rare in the previously isolated phenolic acid derivatives. The two compounds were tested in vitro for neuroprotective activities against 6-OHDA-induced cell death in SH-SY5Y cells, and the result showed that compounds 1 and 2 displayed moderate neuroprotective activity with the IC50 values of 17.4 and 21.3 μM, respectively.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
